            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0613" n="601" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg601"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.91262/203a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-20T18:00:00-05:00">March 20, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>247. A very great amount of anxiety has been created in various circles here
                    because of the arrest of Jay Allen. Mrs. Roosevelt is personally interested in
                    the matter as well as many other prominent persons.</p>
                <p>I shall appreciate it if you will investigate the situation yourself and let me
                    have your judgment as to what, if anything, the Embassy can do to expedite his
                    release. I fully appreciate the circumstances set forth by Barnes in his recent
                    messages, but it may be that you feel that something further can be done.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
